      "created_at": "2019-06-07T14:55:31Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-06-07T14:56:26Z",
      "body": "Just as an addition for other people, who like to use webhooks for Pretix in RocketChat, here is a script, useful to add in the webhook-integrations of Rocket.Chat: \r\n\r\nStep 1: New webhook (fill in everything as you like)\r\nStep 2: Activate script (and please edit [URLOFYOURPRETIXSERVER])\r\n\r\n```\r\nclass Script {\r\n  process_incoming_request({ request }) {\r\n    // console is a global helper to improve debug\r\n    console.log(request.content);\r\n    return {\r\n      content:{\r\n        attachments: [{\r\n          title: \"Ticket \" + request.content.code,\r\n          title_link: 'https://[URLOFYOURPRETIXSERVER]/control/event/' + request.content.organizer + \"/\"+ request.content.event + \"/orders/\" + request.content.code +\"/\",\r\n          text: \"Bestellung eingegangen\",\r\n          fields: [\r\n            {\r\n              title: \"Veranstaltung\",\r\n              value: request.content.event\r\n            },\r\n            {\r\n              title: \"Veranstalter\",\r\n              value: request.content.organizer\r\n            }\r\n          ]\r\n        }]\r\n       }\r\n    };\r\n    return {\r\n       error: {\r\n         success: false,\r\n         message: 'Error'\r\n       }\r\n    };\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\nStep 3: After saving, you will get a webhook-URL, which you have to copy. \r\nStep 4: Log in to pretix: https:/[URLOFYOURPRETIXSERVER]/control/organizers/ (You need to be admin and organizer for the events you want to add to the webhook). \r\nStep 5: Add target-webhook-URL. \r\n\r\nRight now, only new orders work well. If someone knows how to deal with the REST-API, more informations can be added to the chatbot, but be careful with personal data you save in the chat (#GDPR).  \r\n\r\n\r\n",
